# Phase 6, the spending guard with a limit for one fleet: billing reaches
# its own agent-hour and is held alone, with a hold file in its own run; the
# job and the fleet search go on. The person's item counts billing's agents
# and no other's; one more agent-hour lets the fleet go.
agent G1.1: listen
agent G2.1: listen
agent B1.1: listen
agent B2.1: hang
agent S1.1: hang
agent S2.1: hang
file brief.md: Target: the shop | Change: your part | Constraints: none | Ownership: your own files | Acceptance: the check passes
git
orch: init
human: set fleets.mode on
human: set spend.guard on
human: set spend.fleet 1
human: set stuck.watch off
orch: run new "the shop, by fleets"                 -> expect r1
task G1 "Build billing" --name "billing one" --fleet billing --check "exit 0" --brief brief.md
task G2 "Build search" --name "search one" --fleet search --check "exit 0" --brief brief.md
orch: start G1                                      -> expect "(G1.1)"
as-worker G1.1: task add B1 "Refunds" --name "refund flow" --owns refunds.txt --check "exit 0" --brief brief.md
as-worker G1.1: task add B2 "Invoices" --name "invoice pdf" --owns invoice.txt --check "exit 0" --brief brief.md
as-worker G1.1: start B1                            -> expect "(B1.1)"
clock +50m
orch: status --sweep --quiet
orch: wait --timeout 0                              -> expect budget billing
orch: wait --ack last --timeout 0
orch: start G2                                      -> expect "(G2.1)"
as-worker G2.1: task add S1 "The box" --name "search box" --owns search.txt --check "exit 0" --brief brief.md
as-worker G2.1: task add S2 "The ranking" --name ranking --owns rank.txt --check "exit 0" --brief brief.md
as-worker G2.1: start S1                            -> expect "(S1.1)"
clock +10m
orch: status --sweep --quiet
as-worker r2/B1.1: hook gate                        -> expect "agent-hours"
as-worker r3/S1.1: hook gate
as-worker G1.1: start B2                            -> expect exit 5 "spending guard"
as-worker G2.1: start S2                            -> expect "(S2.1)"
orch: status --items                                -> expect "billing has used its 1 agent-hour"
human: status --items --json                        -> expect "1 agent is held"
human: answer n1 more
clock +5s
orch: status --sweep --quiet
as-worker r2/B1.1: hook gate
as-worker r2/B1.1: mail                             -> expect "You were paused"
as-worker G1.1: start B2                            -> expect "(B2.1)"
assert: n1 state used; in r2: attempts B1.1 working, B2.1 working; in r3: attempts S1.1 working, S2.1 working
assert: no event lost; no event twice; in r2: no event lost; in r3: no event lost
